 "applies_to": "BECS Technology BECsys5, BECsys7 and BECsysBW pool/aquatic water chemistry controllers on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
 "summary": "Gateway profile for BECsys controllers: 190 objects (34 AI, 55 AO, 101 BI), all polled. Inputs give product data, clock, general and flow alarms, pH, ORP, free/total/combined chlorine, flow, conductivity/TDS and temperature readings with their feed relay states and high/low/limit alarms, plus inventory levels; outputs set pH, ORP and chlorine set points, spans, alarm points and the SuperChlor, booster and heater set points.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile BECSys_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/BECsys.docx).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "All 190 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
 ],
